Golem: a pseudo-tiled window is hit where it is drawn, not across its tile.

`vectorToWindowUnified` tests a tiled window against its layout box
(`m_position`/`m_size`): right for a window that fills its tile, wrong for a
PSEUDO-tiled one, which sits smaller inside it. Everything around the window
— wallpaper, and on Golem the desktop's icons — then belonged to the window:
a click there focused it and never reached the layer underneath, so the
desktop could not be used on any workspace holding a pseudo window (Max,
2026-10-08: "the desktop always can be used, if I have the room to click
on it").

A pseudo target is now tested against its real box (the goal of
`m_realPosition`/`m_realSize`), grown by the border grab area when input
extents are asked for, so its own edges still resize. The work-area-edge
stretch that follows is for windows that fill their tile and is skipped.
Non-pseudo tiled windows are untouched.

